<note version="0.3" xmlns:link="http://beatniksoftware.com/tomboy/link" xmlns:size="http://beatniksoftware.com/tomboy/size" xmlns="http://beatniksoftware.com/tomboy">
  <title>check RT limits</title>
  
<text xml:space="preserve"><note-content version="0.1">check RT limits

heck the limits

Run:

ulimit -r

If you see:

95

you're good.

If it says:

0

then PAM limits haven't been applied.

Verify MPD

The warning should disappear.

You can also inspect the scheduling policy:

ps -Leo pid,cls,rtprio,pri,ni,cmd | grep mpd

You should eventually see something like:

SCHED_FIFO   50

or

FF 50

for the output thread.

</note-content></text>
